// Refined curved lattice with an OUTER SURFACE (review 27 Oct 2026, #2): a
// restricted (A)20 adsorbing (chi_S -1) on the concave inner wall of a
// spherical, then a cylindrical, pore at FJC_choices 11. Starts 1/3 put the
// wall in the ghost band (`upperbound : surface`, S frozen at upperbound);
// starts 2/4 are the FROZEN-SHELL TWINS: the same pore with n_layers 14, a
// solid S shell on layers 13;14 and a mirror upper bound. A surface is a
// solid region with G = 0, so each pair must agree (rows 1 = 2, 3 = 4, to
// the solver floor: Omega 4e-10 / 1e-9, mu 4e-12 / 4e-11 at creation; the
// lattice-level identity is exact, tests/refined_curved_stencil.py S3).
// Before the fix the outward bonds past the wall were weighted with the
// MIRROR-fold area area(rhigh - k/fjc) instead of their free-space area:
// the concave wall absorbed less than a planar one, Omega -2.3877259
// (sphere, 5 %) and -0.4671533 (cylinder, 20 %) against the twins'
// -2.2694603 / -0.3874513.
// ORACLE-ANCHORED through the twins: Namics 3e9eafd on starts 2/4 gives
// Omega -2.2694603025853626, mu -14.754923587608188 (sphere) and
// Omega -0.387451304515466, mu -8.9572971746124388 (cylinder), equal to
// rows 2/4 to its convergence floor (~1e-9). Namics' own surface wall
// (starts 1/3) reproduces the PRE-FIX PySFBox numbers digit for digit --
// LGrad1.cpp folds every outward channel past MX/fjc regardless of the
// boundary type (:84-93, :101-110 cylinder; :130-139, :147-156 sphere), so
// on this input class the two engines DISAGREE BY DESIGN.
lat : NN : geometry : spherical
lat : NN : n_layers : 12
lat : NN : FJC_choices : 11
lat : NN : lattice_type : hexagonal
lat : NN : upperbound : surface

mon : S : freedom : frozen
mon : S : frozen_range : upperbound
mon : A : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_S : -1.0
mon : A : chi_W : 0.4
mon : W : freedom : free

mol : W : composition : (W)1
mol : W : freedom : solvent
mol : pol : composition : (A)20
mol : pol : freedom : restricted
mol : pol : theta : 200

newton : NN : tolerance : 1e-10

output : kal : append : false
kal : mol : pol : theta
kal : mol : pol : mu
kal : mol : pol : phibulk
kal : sys : NN : free_energy
kal : sys : NN : grand_potential
kal : lat : NN : n_layers
start

lat : NN : n_layers : 14
lat : NN : upperbound : mirror
mon : S : frozen_range : 13;14
start

lat : NN : geometry : cylindrical
lat : NN : n_layers : 12
lat : NN : upperbound : surface
mon : S : frozen_range : upperbound
start

lat : NN : n_layers : 14
lat : NN : upperbound : mirror
mon : S : frozen_range : 13;14
start
